  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "The CVE Program states that the **CVE List** (CVE Records published by partner organizations) is what feeds the NVD. NVD, run by NIST, is a separate program that ingests and enriches those records.\n\n1. **CVE Program — Related Efforts (NVD)**  \n   CVE and NVD are separate. The CVE List, launched by The MITRE Corporation in 1999, “feeds NVD,” which builds on information in CVE Records. NVD was launched by NIST in 2005.  \n   Source: https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts\n\n2. **CVE Program — Program relationships / external partners**  \n   NVD (NIST) is listed as an external partner. “The CVE List feeds NVD,” which has historically added enrichment (for example severity and impact) on top of CVE Records.  \n   Source: https://www.cve.org/ProgramOrganization/ProgramRelationshipwithPartners\n\n3. **CVE Program FAQs — relationship with NVD**  \n   Same official position: the CVE List feeds NVD; NVD is synchronized with and built upon CVE Records. CVE Records are used by many products and services, including NVD.  \n   Source: https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n4. **CVE Program — history**  \n   NIST’s NVD is “synchronized with, and based upon, the CVE List.” CNA partners build the list: “Every CVE Record is added by a CNA.”  \n   Source: https://www.cve.org/about/history\n\n5. **NVD General FAQs (NIST)**  \n   The CVE Program is maintained by the MITRE Corporation and sponsored by DHS/CISA. NVD augments the CVE List and is synchronized so CVE List updates appear in NVD. NVD processes the CVE List about hourly for new publications, rejections, and modifications.  \n   Source: https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/General-FAQs\n\n6. **NVD CVE FAQs (NIST)**  \n   CNAs (and the CVE Assignment Team) assign IDs and publish records to the Official CVE List. NVD then enriches published CVEs (references, CVSS, CWE, CPE, and similar). NVD does not run disclosure or CVE publication.  \n   Source: https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/CVE-FAQs\n\n7. **NVD — CVEs and the NVD process**  \n   The CVE program is maintained by MITRE and sponsored by DHS/CISA. IDs are assigned by MITRE and by CNAs. Published CVE List entries typically appear in NVD within about an hour, after which NVD enrichment can begin.  \n   Source: https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process\n\n8. **CVE List distribution (official downloads)**  \n   Bulk CVE Records in CVE Record Format are the official CVE List (cvelistV5 on GitHub), generated from the CVE Services API—the catalog NVD and others consume.  \n   Source: https://www.cve.org/downloads and https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5\n\n**Bottom line:** The CVE Program identifies the **CVE List**—records published by **CVE Numbering Authorities (CNAs)** under the program operated for the secretariat by **The MITRE Corporation**—as the source that feeds the records NVD uses. NVD (NIST) consumes and enriches that list; it is not the original publisher of CVE Records.",
